node_modules/
# Spine example projects are fetched, not redistributed — see NOTICE.md
examples/
# Reference frames of the one example that ships no upstream license.txt, so its
# images carry no redistribution grant: rendering them locally is allowed (owner
# ruling 2026-08-26, issue #3), committing them never is. `render_reference.ts`
# refuses any --out inside this repository that this line does not cover, so the
# rule is enforced by `git check-ignore` rather than by remembering it.
/bench/reference-local/
# The cut table is the owning project's, not this repository's: it names paths
# into art that lives somewhere else. The selftest never picks one up implicitly
# — point a run at it with `--cuts <path>` or `RIGC_CUTS=<path>` — but a copy is
# convenient to keep here, so it stays ignored.
/cuts.json
.DS_Store
# `npm pack` output, from checking what a publish would ship.
/spine-rigc-*.tgz
# Where `rigc render` and `rigc preview` land by default. Running either from a
# checkout is the normal way to look at something, and neither output belongs to
# this repository — the reference frames that DO live here are under bench/.
/render/
/preview.html
# The gallery's examples ship their SOURCE — parts, rig, motion — and nothing
# built from it. Each README's commands write the skeleton, the frames and the
# preview beside the example so they can be run verbatim from a clean checkout,
# and these lines are what keeps doing that from dirtying the tree.
/gallery/*/build/
/gallery/*/render/
/gallery/*/preview.html
